  "note": "Per-page download budgets for the built site (tools/ci/budgets.py pages). JS/CSS = the files a page's HTML loads, gzip kB; data = files the page fetches at load (globs under site/dist, listed from the page code: FRONTEND keeps them current), gzip kB. Thresholds are 25 % above the sizes measured on 22 Oct 2026, rounded up to 5 kB; raise one only on purpose, in the same commit as the change. Classic <script src> files (the simulator's engine/*.js, copied in by copy-simulator.mjs) count with the page JS; 'lazy' lists the entry chunks a page imports later (their static imports are followed), budgeted as lazy_gzip_kb (simulator set on 22 Oct 2026 at today + 25 %). 3D pages (index, world, world/trace, lab/lander, lab/rover, vehicles, stories) count every file they load once 3D is entered, data and lazy chunks alike, as measured in Chrome on 22 Oct 2026 (F-40), at measured + 5 %: per-sun horizon maps and the per-vendor detect-gpu benchmark are computed globs (the n heaviest matches, n = maps a page or story fetched); /stories/ has one variant per story, each walked through all its steps; lazy_css and fonts as fetched in Chrome on every page; lazy chunks are named <src dir>-<name> (vite.config.js) so each glob matches one chunk. Since B-56 an entry can also use 'computed' ([{glob, count: max|sum, n}], for URLs chosen at run time, added to data), 'variants' ({\"?s=<id>\": {data, computed, lazy, lazy_css, fonts}}, every budget on the heaviest variant), 'lazy_css' + lazy_css_gzip_kb, and 'fonts' + fonts_kb (raw bytes; font preloads always count); unknown keys are errors (tools/ci/budgets.py docstring).",
